    "title": "Bulleit Frontier Whiskey Review - Mesquite Smoked Malt Kentucky Straight Bourbon Whiskey: Wild West meets the smokehouse. - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago Fun fact: their first batch was originally released at what was called Ancient Age, which today is called Buffalo Trace. Eventually, Bulleit would expand production at Seagram after selling the brand in 1997. From there, Seagram produced Bulleit Frontier Whiskey at Four Roses in Lawrenceburg, Kentucky. Owing to the dissolution of Seagrams, Diageo (and Pernod-Ricard) acquired Bulleit and other brands in 2000. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
